                <pb facs="1048" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2799: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-01T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 2—12:04
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your October 27, 4 p.m. through Peking. Final meeting this day abolished
                    Technical Board and all matters will be completed as soon as possible. Since
                    October 15th we have had no direct communication with Vladivostok which is
                    delaying settlement of details. Inter-Allied committee dissolved itself October
                    24th. Copy furnished Peking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
